From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blockchain-Oracle <blockchainoracle.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:24:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: split public transaction sending into prepare and
 sign+submit

`send_pub_tx_with_pre_check` resolves accounts, builds the message, signs
it and submits it in one call. A wallet UI needs to show the user the
exact message (program, accounts, nonces, fee declaration) and get an
approval between building and signing, and must be able to drop the
transaction instead.

Split it into `prepare_public`, returning a `PreparedPublicTx` that
exposes the exact `Message` and its ordered `TxSigner`s, and
`sign_and_submit_public`. `PreparedPublicTx` holds no private keys: local
signing keys are looked up in storage at signing time, keycard signers
carry only their derivation path (and the PIN read during preparation,
as `AccountManager` already did). `send_pub_tx_with_pre_check` is now the
composition of the two, so signatures, their order (local, keycard, then
an external fee co-signer) and all errors are unchanged.

Signing moves from `AccountManager::sign_message` to a free
`account_manager::sign_message` over `TxSigner`s, which the
privacy-preserving path uses too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
